From: qianhui xu <sa226154@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 22:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: libipa: add camera sensor helpers for GC08A8 and S5KJNS

Add gain models and black levels for the two sensors used by the
Lenovo Legion Y700 Gen4 (TB322FC, SM8750):

 - gc08a8 (GalaxyCore, front): raw gain code in 1/1024 steps,
   pedestal 64 at 10 bits.
 - s5kjns (Samsung, rear): raw gain code in 1/32 steps,
   pedestal 64 at 10 bits.

Without these helpers the software ISP interprets the V4L2 analogue
gain code as a multiplier (e.g. code 32 as 32x) and leaves the
black level at zero, so AGC converges to an almost black image.

This lets the sensors keep their natural V4L2 control semantics
(raw gain code) instead of changing the kernel drivers.

Signed-off-by: qianhui xu <sa226154@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
---
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -789,6 +789,38 @@
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov13858", CameraSensorHelperOv13858)
 
+class CameraSensorHelperGc08a8 : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperGc08a8()
+	{
+		/*
+		 * GalaxyCore GC08A8: the V4L2 analogue gain control is the raw
+		 * sensor gain code in 1/1024 steps (0x0400 == 1.0x).
+		 * Pedestal is 64 at 10 bits (see vendor register defaults).
+		 */
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 1024 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("gc08a8", CameraSensorHelperGc08a8)
+
+class CameraSensorHelperS5kjns : public CameraSensorHelper
+{
+public:
+	CameraSensorHelperS5kjns()
+	{
+		/*
+		 * Samsung S5KJNS: the V4L2 analogue gain control is the raw
+		 * sensor gain code in 1/32 steps (0x0020 == 1.0x).
+		 * Pedestal is 64 at 10 bits (see vendor register defaults).
+		 */
+		blackLevel_ = 4096;
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 32 };
+	}
+};
+REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("s5kjns", CameraSensorHelperS5kjns)
+
 class CameraSensorHelperVd55g1 : public CameraSensorHelper
 {
 public:
